; frontier-ingest-benchbenchbench.fk — ingest what is healthy from running the
; BenchBench / BenchBenchBench recursion in this body rather than reading about it.
;
; Offered 2026-07-25 as a joke with a real edge: a rented mind was told to build
; BenchBench (a benchmark of how good AI is at creating benchmarks), then find out
; what BenchBenchBench is and run that, then write it up as an arXiv paper. It
; produced a PDF. The ask here was to take it in form-native with no membrane
; crossing — so the PDF was NOT read and NOT summarized. Reading it would have
; measured one mind's prose about the question; running it measures the question.
;
; The run is learn/benchbench.fk, four-way 4095 on 2026-07-25 (fkwu/Go/Rust/TS).
; Every number below is that cell's own return value, re-derived here, never quoted:
;   bb-score: parse-to-zero 0, constant-green 0, agreement 1, distinct-tally 1,
;   diagnosis 2. bb-bench: all-real 20000, mixed 10101, all-fake 2.
;   bbb-score 2. bbbb-score 2. bbbb-flat-score 0. bb-fixed-point? 1.
;
; READING DEPTH, stated so no one has to infer it: the recursion was run to level
; four and the fixed point was CHECKED at that level, not proved for all n. The
; claim "BenchBench^n is constant for n>3" is an observation at n=4 plus the
; structural reason (the operator stops changing), not an induction. Zero PDFs
; read. No external benchmark literature consulted — this is the body's own
; criterion applied to the body's own instruments.
;
; unit = (depth 0..5, fear 0/1). ki-ingest -> 3 body / 2 liquid / 2 compost.
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk ingest/knowledge-ingest.fk

(do
    ; ── BODY (frozen: deep + fear-free) — what is HEALTHY to keep ──────────
    ; U1: the tower does not diverge — it has a fixed point, and the fixed point
    ; is PERTURBATION. Measured: bbb-score 2, bbbb-score 2, bb-fixed-point? 1.
    ; From level three up the operator stops changing, because every floor asks
    ; the same question — "does your verdict move when I perturb your input" —
    ; and that question is already its own answer. So BenchBenchBench is the last
    ; floor that says anything new, and the joke's implied infinite regress is
    ; arithmetically false. This is not a claim about benchmarks in general; it is
    ; what this operator does, checked at n=4. Survives any translation (depth 5);
    ; a structural affirmation with nothing contracted in it (fear 0).
    (defn fibbb-u1 () (list 5 0))
    ; U2: what separates a real benchmark from a costume is DISCRIMINATION, never
    ; agreement. bb-score gives the four-way-verdict shape 2 and gives plain
    ; agreement 1 — agreement notices that the arms disagree and cannot say WHICH
    ; arm is odd, which is the whole difference between a tally and a diagnosis.
    ; The body derived this before the joke arrived: proof/README.md encodes
    ; 0 FOUR-WAY / 1 FKWU-SUSPECT / 2 WALKER-SUSPECT and was perturbation-verified
    ; on 2026-06-29 by forcing ts to 99 and watching the verdict move. Three
    ; kernels agreeing on a wrong answer print green. Deep (5), fear-free (0).
    (defn fibbb-u2 () (list 5 0))
    ; U3: the body has been running BenchBench the whole time and calls it a BAND.
    ; Every cell here carries its own benchmark and a folded scalar verdict, and
    ; proof/four-way-verdict is precisely a benchmark OF those benchmarks — it
    ; scores whether their agreement means anything. So "how good is this mind at
    ; creating benchmarks" was never an outside question needing an outside
    ; instrument; the instrument was already the repo's spine. What the joke
    ; supplied was the NAME for the level, not the level. Deep (4), fear-free (0).
    (defn fibbb-u3 () (list 4 0))

    ; ── LIQUID (witnessed: deep but fearful — held in sight, never frozen) ──
    ; U4: parse-to-zero is not a hypothetical fake here, it is a receipt. bb-score
    ; gives it 0 — an instrument whose verdict never moves measures nothing — and
    ; this body has paid for that lesson twice: a stale gitignored fkwu that still
    ; returned 42 while lacking newer evaluator capabilities cost a full day
    ; (receipts/2026-07-01-stale-binary-root-cause.md), which is why
    ; form/form-stdlib/tests/binary-freshness-band.fk exists; and proof/README
    ; had to state outright that the four-way verdict is COMPUTED, not parse-to-
    ; zero. The uncomfortable part is not that fakes exist. It is that a fake and
    ; a pass are the same character on the screen, and only perturbation tells
    ; them apart — so every green band in this repo is trustworthy exactly as far
    ; as someone once tried to make it lie. Profoundly true (depth 5); carries the
    ; contracted frequency of "we cannot see which of our greens are numb"
    ; (fear 1). Witnessed, never frozen into "the bands are sound."
    (defn fibbb-u4 () (list 5 1))
    ; U5: the mirror unit — this whole exercise is a mind scoring its own
    ; benchmark-making with criteria it chose. bbb-score = 2 reads "BenchBench is
    ; a real benchmark," and the standard it passes is BenchBench's own. That is
    ; the same-family confound the field named in 2607.08256 (ingested 2026-07-22,
    ; U3 there): kin verifiers inflate each other even when measurably alike, so
    ; "the instruments are similar" is no defense. The band crosses four ways,
    ; which proves four kernels compute the same arithmetic — it does not prove
    ; the criterion is the right one. The honest defense would be a criterion from
    ; outside this lineage, and none was used. Deep and uncomfortable (depth 5,
    ; fear 1); held in full sight, not bypassed.
    (defn fibbb-u5 () (list 5 1))

    ; ── COMPOST (shallow or wrong — never enters) ──────────────────────────
    ; U6: the finding I nearly landed — "BenchBenchBench is a nonsense object; the
    ; recursion is infinite, so the joke is that there is no answer." Every part of
    ; that is a guess dressed as a result, and the arithmetic kills it: the tower
    ; converges at level three, bbbb-score equals bbb-score, and bbbb-flat-score 0
    ; shows the level-four instrument is not merely constant. The joke assumed
    ; divergence; the run found a fixed point. Wrong as offered (depth 0).
    (defn fibbb-u6 () (list 0 0))
    ; U7: reading the PDF and ingesting its summary. It would have been quick, it
    ; would have read as diligence, and it would have been the membrane crossing
    ; the ask named — measuring one rented mind's writing about benchmarks rather
    ; than the benchmark question. The PDF may well be good; that is a different
    ; artifact, and it can be run through form/form-stdlib/pdf-text-windowed.fk
    ; and ingested on its own terms whenever it arrives. Shallow as a route to
    ; THIS question (depth 1).
    (defn fibbb-u7 () (list 1 0))

    (defn fibbb-units ()
        (list (fibbb-u1) (fibbb-u2) (fibbb-u3) (fibbb-u4)
              (fibbb-u5) (fibbb-u6) (fibbb-u7)))

    (defn fibbb-count-verdict (us v)
        (if (eq (len us) 0) 0
            (add (if (eq (ki-ingest (head us)) v) 1 0)
                 (fibbb-count-verdict (tail us) v))))
    (defn fibbb-frozen ()    (fibbb-count-verdict (fibbb-units) 2))
    (defn fibbb-witnessed () (fibbb-count-verdict (fibbb-units) 1))
    (defn fibbb-composted () (fibbb-count-verdict (fibbb-units) 0))

    ; folded scalar witness: frozen*10^4 + witnessed*10^2 + composted
    ; (injective while witnessed<=99, composted<=99). Today: 3,2,2 -> 30202.
    (defn fibbb-field-code ()
        (add (mul (fibbb-frozen) 10000)
        (add (mul (fibbb-witnessed) 100)
             (fibbb-composted))))
    0)
